Twist
=====

Copyright (C) 2026 Chris Burdess

Twist is a transfer client for the GNU system: a library, libtwist, and a
command-line program, twist.  The command line is mostly compatible with
curl's: the options, standard streams and exit status are the same, so that
twist can replace it in scripts.  The library has handles in the style of
curl's easy, multi and share interfaces.

Schemes
-------

Each is a scheme of one transfer engine:

  http, https       HTTP/1, HTTP/2 and HTTP/3
  ws, wss           WebSocket
  ftp, ftps         FTP
  sftp, scp         files over SSH (scp runs over SFTP)
  smtp, smtps       sending mail
  imap, imaps       fetching mail and listing mailboxes
  pop3, pop3s       retrieving mail
  ldap, ldaps       binding and searching, with the result as LDIF
  mqtt, mqtts       subscribing and publishing
  dict              DICT lookups
  gopher, gophers   Gopher
  tftp              TFTP
  file              local files

The schemes with an s added to the protocol's name (https, wss, ftps, smtps,
imaps, pop3s, ldaps, mqtts, gophers) are TLS from the first byte.  None is
upgraded to TLS once it has started, so there is no STARTTLS.  telnet,
rtsp, smb, smbs, rtmp and rtmps are recognised and not implemented; see TODO.

TLS 1.2 and 1.3 and QUIC are quickstep's, and SSH is foxtrot's.  Transfers can
go through HTTP, HTTPS and SOCKS5 proxies (HTTP/3 through a CONNECT-UDP
proxy), and host names can be resolved over DNS-over-QUIC, -TLS and -HTTPS as
well as plain UDP.  The manual is doc/twist.texi ("make info"), and
doc/twist.1 is the short man page.

Dependencies
------------

  - quickstep, installed so that pkg-config can see quickstep.pc
  - foxtrot, the SSH engine, installed so that pkg-config can see foxtrot.pc
  - libgcrypt 1.12.4 or later, which foxtrot needs, and which the loader
    must find ahead of any older system copy (configure checks this)
  - zlib
  - GNU readline, for the twist program only

Build and install
-----------------

  ./bootstrap
  ./configure
  make
  make check
  make install

If quickstep is installed under a prefix pkg-config does not search,
pass that prefix:

  ./configure --with-quickstep=/prefix

The same applies to foxtrot, with --with-foxtrot=/prefix.

See INSTALL for the GNU build instructions, and TODO for what is
not yet implemented.

